      "description": "Watch Burnley vs Notts County highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 8, 2026. The drama of the Carabao Cup was on full display on 2026-08-08 as Burnley and Notts County locked horns in a fiercely contested encounter. Both sides displayed incredible grit and determination, battling for every ball in a match that refused to follow a simple script until the very last kick. Notts County Stun the Hosts The first half saw Burnley attempting to dominate possession, with Zian Flemming and Jacob Bruun Larsen looking lively in the final third. However, they found it difficult to break through a resilient Notts County backline anchored by James Belshaw . The visitors grew in confidence as the half progressed, looking dangerous on the counter-attack. Their persistence paid dividends in the 42nd minute. Callum Roberts found space outside the box after a neat pass from Nick Tsaroulla and unleashed a pinpoint left-footed strike into the bottom right corner. The stunning effort left the home crowd stunned and gave the underdogs a deserved lead heading into the break. Flemming Ignites the Comeback Whatever was said in the Burnley dressing room worked instantly, as the hosts equalized just two minutes after the restart. In the 47th minute, Zian Flemming clinical finish from the center of the box flew into the top right corner following an assist by Marcus Edwards . The equalizer shifted the momentum, and the second half became a flurry of chances for both sides, with Marcus Edwards forcing a big save from James Belshaw and Zeki Amdouni dragging a shot wide. As the clock ticked down, the tension reached a boiling point. Notts County nearly snatched a late winner when Emile Acquah saw his header saved by Max Weiss , while Burnley ’s late pressure resulted in several corners but no winning goal. With the score locked at 1-1 after 90 minutes, the match moved to a penalty shootout. Shootout Heroics and the Decisive Blow In the shootout, Burnley goalkeeper Max Weiss rose to the occasion, producing two vital saves to deny Emile Acquah and Jacob Bedeau . Although Hannibal Mejbri missed his spot-kick, successful conversions from Zian Flemming , Zeki Amdouni , and Mike Trésor kept the pressure on the visitors. It fell to Kyle Walker to provide the final act of the night. The experienced defender stepped up and hammered his penalty into the top left corner to seal a 4-3 shootout victory. The result sees Burnley progress to the next round after a night where they were pushed to the absolute limit by a valiant Notts County ."
